body: "## User goal\n\nAn issue should be able to reference one relevant learning among hundreds on a feature, without retrieving the entire collection or losing the reference when another entry is removed. The requested capability is broader than learnings: a reusable public SDK reference/addressing primitive for item metadata, exposed ergonomically through CLI and other transports.\n\nDo not assume every scalar field needs a generated ID. Distinguish field paths, stable collection-entry identity, and version-pinned historical references. The exact schema is an open design decision.\n\n## Verified on published 2026.10.3\n\nnpm/tag commit: ca6e718707d7a1582f7abc437f5bd88aab156dfd. Isolated synthetic tracker, no real project data changed.\n\n1. Create a Feature through `PmClient.create`.\n2. Append two learnings through `pm.learnings(id, {add: ...})`.\n3. The second add receipt reports `mutation_receipt.entry_index: 2`; the learning contains `created_at`, `author`, and `text`, without a stable per-entry ID.\n4. Delete learning 1 with `pm.learnings(id, {delete: 1})`.\n5. The target learning is now position 1, preserving timestamp/text but still without an entry ID.\n\nThe current CLI exposes edit/delete by one-based index and latest-N/full-history reads; the public options do not expose an entry-ID selector. The top-level result `id` is the owning item ID, not the learning ID.\n\nAn illustrative dependency target `feature-id#learnings/2` is rejected with `dependency_target_not_found`; this is not documented syntax and is included only to distinguish arbitrary fragment strings from a supported resolver. Generic in-memory graph node strings do not themselves provide persisted metadata reference resolution.\n\nSources: [LogNote and Comment shapes](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/blob/ca6e718707d7a1582f7abc437f5bd88aab156dfd/src/types.ts), [shared annotation contracts](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/blob/ca6e718707d7a1582f7abc437f5bd88aab156dfd/src/sdk/annotations.ts), [learnings public operation](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/blob/ca6e718707d7a1582f7abc437f5bd88aab156dfd/src/sdk/learnings.ts).\n\n## Proposed acceptance\n\n- Define a reusable SDK contract to address and resolve metadata fields, collection entries, and supported fragments; expose equivalent agent-oriented CLI behavior.\n- Permit relationships/evidence references to target the specific referenced value, with owning item/workspace provenance.\n- Collection-entry references remain stable when unrelated entries are inserted, deleted, reordered, or merged. Define edit semantics and distinguish live identity from immutable/version-pinned content.\n- Selective resolution returns only the requested content plus explicit provenance/version and missing/deleted/ambiguous status, within normal output budgets.\n- Preserve compatibility for existing `.toon` and JSONL history, including import, copy, restore, branch merge, and redaction. Do not silently reidentify old records or fabricate historical identities.\n- Cover learnings as the concrete regression fixture and evaluate comments, notes, evidence and structured custom metadata without assuming they all have identical requirements.\n- Keep primitives harness-independent and configurable; no per-learning bespoke command family or forced human-centric syntax.\n\n## Scope and duplicate check\n\nThis is an enhancement grounded in a runtime identity limitation, not a claim that all metadata operations are broken. Searched open/closed GitHub issues and all-status tracked items for annotation identity, learning references, entry IDs, metadata addressability and fragments. Existing annotation output receipts, grammar consolidation, history reconstruction, and whole-item relationships are related but do not establish this fine-grained reference contract.\n\nRelated existing owner: [Storage, history and data durability](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/blob/main/.agents/pm/epics/pm-o2kc.toon). Please link a canonical implementation PM item during local-agent intake; no new checkout item was created here, preserving the active local writer's ownership."
